---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import { repository } from '../data/site';
---
<section class="details-section section-space wrap"><div class="section-heading reveal"><p class="eyebrow">FEELS RIGHT AT HOME</p><h2>Made for Mac.<br /><span class="muted-heading">Down to the little things.</span></h2></div><div class="details-grid"><article class="reveal"><span class="detail-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⌘</span><h3>Native, through and through.</h3><p>Built with SwiftUI and real Liquid Glass. A natural extension of your desktop, with the feel you already love.</p></article><article class="reveal"><span class="detail-symbol" aria-hidden="true">↘</span><h3>There when you need it.</h3><p>A floating bar that keeps your essentials close. Auto-hide lets your work take the whole stage.</p></article><article class="reveal"><span class="detail-symbol" aria-hidden="true">&lt;/&gt;</span><h3>Yours to make better.</h3><p>Open source from the start. Explore the code, contribute a native widget, or help shape what comes next.</p></article></div><a class="text-link source-link reveal" href={repository}>Take a look under the hood <Icon size={18} /></a></section>
<section id="get-started" class="get-started wrap reveal"><span class="eyebrow">A LITTLE CHANGE TO YOUR EVERYDAY</span><h2>Make yourself <span class="serif-accent">at home.</span></h2><p>Your Mac has room for a little more you.</p><a href={`${repository}/releases`} class="button button-primary"><Icon name="download" size={18} /> Get OpenDock</a><span class="download-note">For macOS 26 and later · Free & open source</span><p class="release-note">Early days, thoughtfully built. Check GitHub for available releases<br class="desktop-break" /> or <a href={repository}>build from source</a> to try the latest.</p><span class="cta-spark" aria-hidden="true">✳</span></section>
<section class="faq-section wrap section-space"><div class="reveal"><p class="eyebrow">A FEW LITTLE ANSWERS</p><h2>Good to know.</h2></div><div class="faq-list reveal"><details><summary>What do I need to run OpenDock?<span>+</span></summary><p>OpenDock is a native Mac app for macOS 26 and later. Check the repository’s releases for available builds and installation details.</p></details><details><summary>Does it replace the macOS Dock?<span>+</span></summary><p>OpenDock adds a personal space for widgets and launchers. It doesn’t replace the system Dock’s window management, minimized windows, or Exposé.</p></details><details><summary>Can I build my own widgets?<span>+</span></summary><p>Yes. Native widgets use the Swift SDK in OpenDockKit. JavaScript and React widgets, along with a community marketplace, are on the roadmap.</p></details><details><summary>Is OpenDock free?<span>+</span></summary><p>OpenDock is free and open source. You can explore the code, report an issue, and contribute on GitHub.</p></details></div></section>
